{"aliases": ["PyTorch, TensorFlow, JAX all build one under the hood"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_e13416b3fc", "name": "Computational graph is universal in autodiff", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Computational Graphs (Autodiff).md", "message": "This is the universal data structure that powers every autodiff system", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "PyTorch, TensorFlow, and JAX all build a computational graph under the hood, making the computational graph the universal data structure of autodiff systems."}
{"aliases": ["Two features are conditionally independent given a class if knowing one feature tells you nothing about the other, once the class is known."], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_8eb8ab836f", "name": "Conditional independence definition", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Conditional Independence.md", "message": "Definition", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "Two features are conditionally independent given a class when, once the class is known, knowing one feature tells you nothing about the other."}
