{"aliases": ["A prior is conjugate when prior and posterior belong to the same distribution family", "no integrals, no sampling"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_5db6cf7065", "name": "Conjugate prior definition", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Conjugate Priors.md", "message": "The Idea", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "A prior is conjugate when the prior and the posterior belong to the same distribution family, which makes the update algebraically trivial with no integrals and no sampling."}
