{"aliases": ["Mean = a/(a+b)", "The sum a+b is your effective sample size"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_672d44e377", "name": "Beta parameters as effective sample size", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Conjugate Priors.md", "message": "Beta(1,1) gives a+b=2 (low confidence, wide spread across [0,1]); Beta(100,100) gives a+b=200 (high confidence, narrow peak tightly concentrated at 0.5).", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "Beta(a, b) is bounded on [0,1] with mean a/(a+b), and the sum a+b acts as the effective sample size that sets how much weight the prior carries."}
