{"aliases": ["each production rule maps a single non-terminal symbol to a string of terminals and non-terminals", "the rule applies regardless of surrounding context"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_2aed8cc303", "name": "Context-free grammar definition", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Context-Free Grammar (CFG).md", "message": "A **context-free grammar** is a formal grammar where each production rule maps a single non-terminal symbol to a string of terminals and non-terminals.", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "A context-free grammar is a formal grammar in which each production rule maps a single non-terminal symbol to a string of terminals and non-terminals, and the rule applies regardless of surrounding context."}
