{"aliases": ["A convolution slides a small filter (kernel) across the image.", "The result is a feature map"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_53ebf155a2", "name": "Convolution operation definition", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Convolution Operation.md", "message": "A **convolution** slides a small filter (kernel) across the image.", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "A convolution slides a small filter (kernel) across an image, multiplying filter values by the overlapping image pixels and summing them to produce a feature map whose bright spots show where the filter detected its pattern."}
{"aliases": ["a 256×256×3 image → 196,608 inputs → 196M params for one hidden layer"], "createdAt": "2026-10-25T23:18:36Z", "id": "n_b95a3e0822", "name": "Fully-connected image layer parameter blowup", "op": "define", "provenance": [{"file": "Knowledge Wiki/wiki/Convolution Operation.md", "message": "Too many parameters", "session": "backfill-2026-10-26"}], "statement": "A fully-connected network on a 256x256x3 image takes 196,608 inputs and about 196 million parameters for a single hidden layer."}
